The Oyapock River Bridge is a cable-stayed bridge. It crosses the Oyapock River to connect the town of Oiapoque in Brazil with Saint-Georges de l'Oyapock in French Guiana.
An 83-meter-high, two-story building, it is 378 meters long and has two lanes, each 3.50 meters wide.
The vertical clearance under the bridge is 15 meters. Construction was completed in August 2011, but the bridge did not open to traffic until March 2017.
This bridge is scheduled to open for official use in September 2017, when the Brazilian border checkpoint is expected to be completed.
